lly lose $563 million in liquidations as Ether and Bitcoin lead losses\\\",\\n  \\\"primary_asset\\\": \\\"Bitcoin\\\",\\n  \\\"chart_coin\\\": \\\"bitcoin\\\",\\n  \\\"sources_used\\\": [\\n    \\\"CoinDesk\\\",\\n    \\\"Google News\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"source_urls\\\": [\\n    \\\"https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/crypto-traders-betting-on-a-rally-lose-usd563-million-in-liquidations-ether-and-bitcoin-suffer-the-most\\\",\\n    \\\"https://news.google.?oc=5\\\",\\n    \\\"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivwFBVV95cUxPaFB0VnhqRmROaDR3M0w5S2c5RmU0WW9UcFQwUkJFRDJvRXU1Z3VQU2RNaVBRZDlCSFNmQWNTNi12SEl6Z2xrRjJ2Mkp6cUN2LUdFdjJsbDNoc0FDVnRiWE5oancycjZKcmpPQ28xdXJweG9Gb0ZFd01ZaU9pdFpxdjB4RHZ2ZGE1c1Zxay1tVDEzNWgwcFVVLXRBSDNlZUFSdWF4UmFXdlRDTUZ2ZVlpQkZkRlloMXJaMnV3X3U4Yw?oc=5\\\",\\n    \\\"https://news.google.?oc=5\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"combined_key_facts\\\": [\\n    \\\"CoinDesk’s feed summary says crypto traders betting on a rally lost $563 million in liquidations, with Ether and Bitcoin suffering the most.\\\",\\n    \\\"A Google News item mirroring Bloomberg’s coverage says Bitcoin hit a two-week low as crypto liquidations topped half a billion.\\\",\\n    \\\"Other same-day related headlines describe Bitcoin falling to about $76.7K and say the selloff triggered roughly $661 million in liquidations, reinforcing that leveraged longs were the main casualty.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aggregated_raw_content\\\": \\\"On Mon, 18 May 2026, the dominant crypto news event across the feeds was a sharp market selloff that triggered a large wave of liquidations, with Bitcoin and Ether leading the damage. CoinDesk’s feed headline was explicit: “Crypto traders betting on a rally lose $563 million in liquidations. Ether and bitcoin suffer the most.” Its summary said Ether and bitcoin led liquidations as their prices dropped on macroeconomic concerns. Another CoinDesk item published the same morning framed the move as “Bitcoin slides under $77,000 as oil shock and Treasury yields hit risk assets,” adding context that long-term holders were still sitting tight and exchange balances remained near six-year lows, while underwater short-term holders left BTC vulnerable.\\\\n\\\\nThe same event was echoed in Google News results from multiple outlets. One headline read: “Bitcoin (BTC) Hits Two-Week Low as Crypto Liquidations Top Half a Billion - Bloomberg.com.” Another same-day result said: “Bitcoin falls to two-week low of $76.7K as crypto market selloff triggers $661 million liquidations - The Economic Times.” A further related headline said: “$660M Liquidated as Bitcoin Crashes on Trump-Iran Escalation Fears - CryptoPotato.” Yet another reported: “Today in Crypto: Bitcoin Price Dips to $76K, Ethereum Leads $650M Liquidation Flush on Weekend - The Crypto Times.” The Google News feed also surfaced a separate but closely related story: “Crypto traders betting on a rally lose $563 million in liquidations. Ether and bitcoin suffer the most - CoinDesk,” confirming that the liquidation theme was being widely covered by multiple outlets on the same day.\\\\n\\\\nThe related headlines point to a common pattern: leveraged longs were getting wiped out as risk assets sold off together. The CoinDesk summary says the drop was tied to macroeconomic concerns, while another CoinDesk headline linked the move to oil shock and Treasury yields. The Google News results show the broader press framing it as a market-wide risk-off move, with Bitcoin making a fresh two-week low and liquidations ranging from “half a billion” to roughly “$661 million” depending on the source and timestamp.\\\\n\\\\nA separate Google News cluster also included the CoinDesk piece itself as a mirrored item and a Bloomberg item focused on Bitcoin’s two-week low. Taken together, the coverage shows a unified market narrative: traders who were positioned for a rebound were forced out, Ether and Bitcoin were hit hardest, and the liquidation cascade became the biggest crypto market event of the day.\\\\n\\\\nThe extracted text available from the RSS layer is limited, but the feed snippets consistently describe the same event: a broad crypto downturn, heavy liquidations, Bitcoin under pressure near the mid-$70,000s, and Ether among the worst performers. CoinDesk’s wording emphasizes the size of the wipeout and the fact that traders betting on a rally bore the brunt. Google News adds corroborating headlines from Bloomberg, The Economic Times, CryptoPotato, and The Crypto Times, all pointing to the same high-volatility selloff and its liquidation consequences.\\\"\\n}\"],\"finalPromptText\":\"[Mon 2026-05-18 08:59 UTC] Follow your SOUL to cross-reference multiple RSS feeds, find the single biggest news event, and extract deep facts. Return ONLY the aggregated JSON with ALL required fields — no prose outside the JSON block.\",\"messagesSnapshot\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"[Mon 2026-05-18 08:59 UTC] Follow your SOUL to cross-reference multiple RSS feeds, find the single biggest news event, and extract deep facts. Return ONLY the aggregated JSON with ALL required fields — no prose outside the JSON block.\"}],\"timestamp\":1779094762851},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"call_Uof48lVEi6uWBZv2unPt0b9M\",\"name\":\"exec\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"python - <<'PY'\\nimport feedparser, sys, requests, datetime, time\\nfeeds = {\\n'CoinDesk':'https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/',\\n'CoinTelegraph':'https://c\n\n⚠️ [... middle content omitted — showing head and tail ...]\n\ng-with-sec?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=<redacted> -> show first 80 lines (+1 steps) (in ~/.openclaw/workspace-researcher), `curl -sL 'https://cointelegraph.com/news/blockchaincom-confidentially-submits-ipo-filing-with-sec?utm_source=rss_feed&u…`\"},{\"toolName\":\"web_search\",\"meta\":\"for \\\"\\\"Blockchain.com\\\" confidential submission draft registration statement proposed initial public offe