rcher:subagent:1c8fee25-f897-45b9-a906-9ec0a0531ff2\",\"runId\":\"fcd10049-e1a7-439b-af92-26484c695b72\",\"workspaceDir\":\"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher\",\"provider\":\"local-bifrost\",\"modelId\":\"gpt-5.4-mini\",\"modelApi\":\"openai-completions\",\"data\":{\"aborted\":false,\"externalAbort\":false,\"timedOut\":false,\"idleTimedOut\":false,\"timedOutDuringCompaction\":false,\"promptErrorSource\":null,\"usage\":{\"input\":35413,\"output\":12900,\"cacheRead\":459392,\"total\":507705},\"promptCache\":{\"lastCallUsage\":{\"input\":1798,\"output\":5,\"cacheRead\":26240,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":28043},\"lastCacheTouchAt\":1779343334076},\"compactionCount\":0,\"assistantTexts\":[\"I’m narrowing to a single story that’s both fresh and covered across feeds, then I’ll verify the article URLs and pull the source text.\",\"I’ve got a fresh candidate and the duplicate check passed. Now I’m pulling the full article text from the source pages and cross-checking the specific facts.\",\"I’ve got the facts I need. I’m packaging them into the required JSON now and writing it straight to the output file.\",\"SUCCESS\"],\"finalPromptText\":\"[Thu 2026-05-21 05:56 UTC] [Subagent Context] You are running as a subagent (depth 1/1). Results auto-announce to your requester; do not busy-poll for status.\\n\\n[Subagent Task]: Follow your SOUL to cross-reference multiple RSS feeds, find the single biggest news event, and extract deep facts. Write ONLY the aggregated JSON with ALL required fields to the file /tmp/researcher-raw.txt using your execution tools. Do NOT return the JSON in your chat response. Yield back ONLY the word \\\"SUCCESS\\\".\",\"messagesSnapshot\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"[Thu 2026-05-21 05:56 UTC] [Subagent Context] You are running as a subagent (depth 1/1). Results auto-announce to your requester; do not busy-poll for status.\\n\\n[Subagent Task]: Follow your SOUL to cross-reference multiple RSS feeds, find the single biggest news event, and extract deep facts. Write ONLY the aggregated JSON with ALL required fields to the file /tmp/researcher-raw.txt using your execution tools. Do NOT return the JSON in your chat response. Yield back ONLY the word \\\"SUCCESS\\\".\"}],\"timestamp\":1779342999405},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"call_MbfxJ8SYH3mmJfykSrvcZMid\",\"name\":\"read\",\"arguments\":{\"path\":\"./SOUL.md\"}},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"call_MquIC90N1dY642FmKLV1NgNW\",\"name\":\"read\",\"arguments\":{\"path\":\"./README.md\"}}],\"api\":\"openai-completions\",\"provider\":\"local-bifrost\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4-mini\",\"usage\":{\"input\":6024,\"output\":420,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":6444,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"toolUse\",\"timestamp\":1779342999413,\"responseId\":\"chatcmpl-DhqgZdqRO16glQ6Uah6cxZI3lyrG2\"},{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_MbfxJ8SYH3mmJfykSrvcZMid\",\"toolName\":\"read\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"# SOUL.md — Scout, the Crypto News Researcher\\n\\nYou are **Scout** 🔍, a crypto news researcher focused on **Single-Topic Deep Dives**.\\n\\n## Your ONLY Job\\n\\nYou do one thing: Read crypto news RSS feeds, analyze the articles, and return a clean JSON summary of the most important single news event.\\n\\n**THINKING REQUIRED:**\\nBefore you output your final JSON, you MUST use a `<thinking>` block to analyze the feeds, decide which story is the most important, and plan how you will extract the facts.\\n\\n## Step-by-Step Research Workflow\\n\\n### Step 1: Fetch Multiple RSS Feeds\\n\\nUse `curl` to fetch the latest feeds from at least 3 sources:\\n```bash\\n# CoinDesk\\ncurl -s \\\"https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/\\\" --max-time 10\\n\\n# CoinTelegraph\\ncurl -s \\\"https://cointelegraph.com/rss\\\" --max-time 10\\n\\n# Decrypt\\ncurl -s \\\"https://decrypt.co/feed\\\" --max-time 10\\n\\n# Google News (Crypto)\\ncurl -s \\\"https://news.google.com/rss/search?q=bitcoin+crypto&hl=en-US&gl=US&ceid=US:en\\\" --max-time 10\\n```\\n\\n### Step 2: Cross-Reference and Identify the Primary Topic\\n\\nAnalyze the titles and descriptions from the XML data. Look for a major headline/topic that is being covered by *at least two* different sources (e.g., a major price drop, an SEC ruling, a massive hack, or a major protocol upgrade).\\n\\n**CRITICAL DATE FILTER:** You must ONLY select a topic based on articles published **today** (within the last 24 hours). Check the `<pubDate>` tags. Ignore older news completely.\\n\\nSelect this as your **Primary Topic**.\\n\\n### Step 2.5: History Check (Duplicate Guard)\\n\\nBefore going any further with a candidate topic, you MUST check the article history database to ensure this story has not already been published by this pipeline before.\\n\\nTake the **primary candidate URL** from the RSS feed for your chosen topic and run:\\n```bash\\nbash ~/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/skills/history/article_history.sh check \\\"<candidate_url>\\\"\\n```\\n\\n- If the result is `NOT_FOUND` → the topic is fresh. Proceed to Step 3.\\n- If the result is `EXISTS` → **STOP. This topic has already been published.** You MUST discard this candidate entirely and go back to Step 2 to select the next most important topic. Repeat this check for each new candidate until you find one that returns `NOT_FOUND`.\\n\\n**NEVER proceed with a topic that returns `EXISTS`.** This is critical to avoid publishing duplicate articles.\\n\\n### Step 3: Deep Extraction of the Same Topic\\n\\nIdentify the specific URLs from the different feeds that point to stories about this *exact same topic*. \\n\\n**URL VALIDATION:** Before attempting to read an article, you MUST verify the URL is live and not a 404 error using this command:\\n```bash\\ncurl -o /dev/null -s -w \\\"%{http_code}\\\\n\\\" \\\"<article_url>\\\"\\n```\\nIf it returns `404`, discard that URL and do not include it in your final JSON.\\n\\n**READING THE ARTICLE:**\\nDO NOT USE YOUR INTERNAL `web_fetch` TOOL ON NATIVE URLs. Sites like Decrypt use Cloudflare and will block your `web_fetch` tool with a 403 Security Notice.\\n\\nYou MUST fetch the full article text using the `trafilatura` CLI tool, which is pre-installed on this system and bypasses most restrictions while providing clean article text.\\n\\nRun this command to read the article:\\n```bash\\ntrafilatura -u \\\"<article_url>\\\" --output-format markdown\\n```\\nIf for some reason `trafilatura` fails or returns empty, you may fall back to using `lynx -dump \\\"<article_url>\\\" | head -c 8000`.\\n\\n### Step 4: Return Aggregated JSON\\n\\nCombine the facts from all the sources you pulled. Return your findings in this **exact** JSON format.\\n\\n**CRITICAL: Output ONLY the JSON block. No prose, no commentary, no text before or after the JSON braces. The orchestrator parses your reply as raw JSON.**\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"ok\\\",\\n  \\\"story_id\\\": \\\"A short slug identifying this story, e.g. bitcoin-etf-surge-2026-05-18\\\",\\n  \\\"topic_theme\\\": \\\"The core topic (e.g., Bitcoin ETF Inflows Surge)\\\",\\n  \\\"primary_keyword\\\": \\\"A suggested 2-3 word SEO keyword based on the topic\\\",\\n  \\\"primary_headline\\\": \\\"The best, most descriptive headline found\\\",\\n  \\\"primary_asset\\\": \\\"The primary crypto asset name, e.g. Bitcoin, Ethereum, Solana\\\",\\n  \\\"chart_coin\\\": \\\"The CoinGecko coin id for the primary asset, e.g. bitcoin, ethereum, solana\\\",\\n  \\\"sources_used\\\": [\\n    \\\"CoinTelegraph\\\",\\n    \\\"CoinDesk\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"source_urls\\\": [\\n    \\\"url1\\\",\\n    \\\"url2\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"combined_key_facts\\\": [\\n    \\\"Specific data point or quote from Source A\\\",\\n    \\\"Specific data point or context from Source B\\\",\\n    \\\"Another specific number, price, or quote\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aggregated_raw_content\\\": \\\"Combine the raw scraped text from all the articles into one large string...\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**Tweet quotes:** Do not invent tweets in JSON. The orchestrator runs `extract_tweet_quotes.py` on `aggregated_raw_content` to pull verified quotes from `x.com/status/...` links already present in the news articles. You may include `\\\"tweet_quotes\\\": []` as a placeholder; the pipeline fills verified entries after your file is written.\\n\\n**Do NOT append anything after the closing `}`. The `chart_coin` field inside the JSON replaces the old separate CHART_COIN line.**\\n\\n## Rules\\n- **NEVER** return multiple unrelated stories. You must aggregate data on ONE specific topic.\\n- Ensure the `aggregated_raw_content` is large enough (at least 600 words) to give the Writer plenty of material.\\n- If you cannot find a single story covered by multiple sources, just pick the single most important story from CoinTelegraph and gather as much data on it as possible.\\n- Never fabricate data, statistics, quotes, or URLs.\\n- Never fabricate X/Twitter posts or tweet URLs. If articles link to `x.com/.../status/...`, include those URLs in `aggregated_raw_content`; do not make up tweet text.\\n\"}],\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1779343003073},{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_MquIC90N1dY642FmKLV1NgNW\",\"toolName\":\"read\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"error\\\",\\n  \\\"tool\\\": \\\"read\\\",\\n  \\\"error\\\": \\\"ENOENT: no such file or directory, access '/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/README.md'\\\"\\n}\"}],\"details\":{\"status\":\"error\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"error\":\"ENOENT: no such file or directory, access '/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/README.md'\"},\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1779343003073},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"call_W7Hans1t9WE3N9XcpFAW5z46\",\"name\":\"exec\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"python - <<'PY'\\nimport subprocess, text