\n\\n### Valid\\n- send progress update\\n- immediately launch next command\\n- or immediately continue polling a running command\\n\\n### Invalid\\n- send progress update\\n- end turn\\n- nothing i\\n\\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L557-L633\",\"source\":\"memory\",\"citation\":\"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L557-L633\",\"corpus\":\"memory\"},{\"id\":\"2285923d57b28a4ede63d1e5e1c171d55ba73cdab477c0fc561036eea2acdf07\",\"path\":\"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md\",\"startLine\":1226,\"endLine\":1283,\"score\":1,\"textScore\":0.8340590754891496,\"snippet\":\"assistant: [[reply_to_current]] Absolutely — here’s a **developer checklist** for fixing the continuous-run behavior.\\n\\n# Developer Checklist — Continuous Crypto Pipeline\\n\\n## A. Workflow ownership\\n- [ ] Define the pipeline as **one active workflow**, not a series of unrelated chat replies\\n- [ ] Ensure one component clearly owns the run from **Step 0 through Step 5**\\n- [ ] Ensure Step 6 is only triggered from explicit user confirmation\\n- [ ] Prevent chat-turn boundaries from acting like implicit stop points\\n\\n---\\n\\n## B. State machine\\n- [ ] Add explicit run status values:\\n  - [ ] `idle`\\n  - [ ] `active`\\n  - [ ] `awaiting_user_confirmation`\\n  - [ ] `blocked_approval`\\n  - [ ] `blocked_error`\\n  - [\\n\\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L1226-L1283\",\"source\":\"memory\",\"citation\":\"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L1226-L1283\",\"corpus\":\"memory\"},{\"id\":\"5f402966a40c3a41d487c6e66ea0bc8b33f944dcf17111a5ef0320182fd541d9\",\"path\":\"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md\",\"startLine\":495,\"endLine\":571,\"score\":1,\"textScore\":0.7812832190321197,\"snippet\":\"- `awaiting_user_confirmation`\\n\\nEverything else means the orchestrator must keep driving.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 4) Manifest spec\\n\\nThe manifest should become the single source of truth.\\n\\n## 4.1 Required top-level fields\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"run_id\\\": \\\"...\\\",\\n  \\\"run_dir\\\": \\\"...\\\",\\n  \\\"created_at\\\": \\\"...\\\",\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"active\\\",\\n  \\\"current_step\\\": \\\"research\\\",\\n  \\\"next_step\\\": \\\"write_article\\\",\\n  \\\"user_input_required\\\": false,\\n  \\\"approval_required\\\": false,\\n  \\\"last_progress_at\\\": \\\"...\\\",\\n  \\\"active_process\\\": null,\\n  \\\"steps\\\": {},\\n  \\\"artifacts\\\": {},\\n  \\\"checks\\\": {},\\n  \\\"results\\\": {},\\n  \\\"errors\\\": []\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4.2 Required per-step structure\\n```json\\n\\\"steps\\\": {\\n  \\\"research\\\": {\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"succeeded\\\",\\n    \\\"started_at\\\": \\\"...\\\",\\n    \\\"f\\n\\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L495-L571\",\"source\":\"memory\",\"citation\":\"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L495-L571\",\"corpus\":\"memory\"}],\"provider\":\"none\",\"citations\":\"auto\",\"debug\":{\"backend\":\"builtin\",\"effectiveMode\":\"n/a\",\"searchMs\":42,\"hits\":5}},\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1779346707308}}\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/agents/orchestrator/sessions/3d69fc49-c0a3-4f8a-ac4e-6e441c7d595d.checkpoint.f701932a-c8a8-48d6-9f48-a64b1009257c.jsonl-192-{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"bec60e35\",\"parentId\":\"c003f475\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-21T06:59:16.669Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Yes — and I think there’s a pretty clean migration path.\\n\\nMy suggestion is to replace the current “shared `/tmp` files as truth” model with a **run-bundle model**, while keeping a thin compatibility layer during transition.\\n\\n## My recommended target design\\n\\n### 1. Make `RUN_DIR` the only source of truth\\nFor each pipeline run:\\n\\n- `/tmp/crypto-run-<RUN_ID>/manifest.json`\\n- `/tmp/crypto-run-<RUN_ID>/research/raw.json`\\n- `/tmp/crypto-run-<RUN_ID>/research/validated.json`\\n- `/tmp/crypto-run-<RUN_ID>/article/raw.md`\\n- `/tmp/crypto-run-<RUN_ID>/article/final.md`\\n- `/tmp/crypto-run-<RUN_ID>/article/article.docx`\\n- `/tmp/crypto-run-<RUN_ID>/media/feature.jpg`\\n- `/tmp/crypto-run-<RUN_ID>/media/chart.png`\\n- `/tmp/crypto-run-<RUN_ID>/publish/google-drive.json`\\n- `/tmp/crypto-run-<RUN_ID>/publish/wordpress.json`\\n\\nThat gives every step one home and one lineage.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Separate “raw” from “validated/final”\\nRight now one big problem is that raw outputs and downstream outputs are mixed loosely.\\n\\nBetter:\\n\\n- researcher writes to `research/raw.json`\\n- validator writes `research/validated.json`\\n- writer reads only `research/validated.json`\\n- writer writes `article/raw.md`\\n- sanitizer/validator writes `article/final.md`\\n- docx is built only from `article/final.md`\\n\\nThat prevents confusion like:\\n- raw updated\\n- final not updated\\n- docx still older\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Stop using global fixed files as authoritative\\nThese are the dangerous ones from what we observed:\\n\\n- `/tmp/researcher-raw.txt`\\n- `/tmp/crypto-article-raw.md`\\n- `/tmp/crypto-article.docx`\\n\\nMy advice:\\n- **do not delete them immediately**\\n- **demote them to compatibility aliases only**\\n- they should never be the canonical truth\\n\\nMeaning:\\n- canonical file lives in `RUN_DIR`\\n- optional old path can symlink to it for backward compatibility\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Make every subagent write into the run directory explicitly\\nInstead of:\\n- `/tmp/researcher-raw.txt`\\n- `/tmp/crypto-article-raw.md`\\n\\npass paths like:\\n- `/tmp/crypto-run-20260521-055616/research/raw.json`\\n- `/tmp/crypto-run-20260521-055616/article/raw.md`\\n\\nThis is the most important behavioral change.\\n\\nBecause otherwise you still have cross-run contamination.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Put the active paths in the manifest\\nThe manifest should be the routing table, not just a note.\\n\\nLike:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"run_id\\\": \\\"20260521-055616\\\",\\n  \\\"run_dir\\\": \\\"/tmp/crypto-run-20260521-055616\\\",\\n  \\\"current_step\\\": \\\"write\\\",\\n  \\\"story\\\": {\\n    \\\"headline\\\": \\\"...\\\",\\n    \\\"slug\\\": \\\"...\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"artifacts\\\": {\\n    \\\"research_raw\\\": \\\".../research/raw.json\\\",\\n    \\\"research_validated\\\": \\\".../research/validated.json\\\",\\n    \\\"article_raw\\\": \\\".../article/raw.md\\\",\\n    \\\"article_final\\\": \\\".../article/final.md\\\",\\n    \\\"docx\\\": \\\".../article/article.docx\\\",\\n    \\\"feature_image\\\": \\\".../media/feature.jpg\\\",\\n    \\\"chart\\\": \\\".../media/chart.png\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThen every validator and downstream step reads from manifest-defined paths, not hardcoded `/tmp/foo`.\\n\\nThis lines up with the “manifest as single source of truth” direction I found in memory too. Source: `memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L495-L571`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Keep transitional symlinks only for legacy compatibility\\nDuring migration, you can still expose:\\n\\n- `/tmp/research.json` -> current run validated research\\n- `/tmp/crypto-article.md` -> current run final article\\n- `/tmp/chart.png` -> current run chart\\n- `/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg` -> current run feature image\\n\\nThat part is fine.\\n\\nWhat I would **not** keep as loose real files:\\n- `/tmp/crypto-article-raw.md`\\n- `/tmp/researcher-raw.txt`\\n- `/tmp/crypto-article.docx`\\n\\nIf old scripts need them, make them symlinks too, not standalone files.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Add step guards that verify artifact freshness\\nEven with folders, I’d still add logic like:\\n\\nBefore Step 2:\\n- validated research exists\\n- it belongs to current `run_id`\\n\\nBefore Step 4:\\n- final article exists\\n- docx was built after final article\\n- docx path matches current run\\n\\nBefore publish:\\n- publish step confirms the exact source file path from manifest\\n\\nThat protects against partial retries and stale leftovers.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Practical migration plan\\n\\n## Option A: safest phased migration\\nThis is what I’d recommend.\\n\\n### Phase 1: Introduce run-dir canonicals\\n- keep current pipeline behavior mostly intact\\n- start writing canonical files inside `RUN_DIR`\\n- keep old `/tmp/...` paths as symlinks to the new canonical files\\n\\n### Phase 2: Update every step to read/write only run-dir paths\\n- researcher writes to run-dir raw file\\n- writer writes to run-dir raw file\\n- validators emit run-dir validated/final files\\n- docx builds from run-dir final file\\n\\n### Phase 3: Remove dependency on old hardcoded global files\\n- old paths remain optional compatibility links only\\n- no validator/publisher should rely on them internally\\n\\n### Phase 4: Remove legacy paths if nothing depends on them\\nOnly after verifying all agents/scripts/publishers use manifest/run-dir paths.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Option B: full cutover\\nYou could change everything at once.\\n\\nI don’t recommend that unless you can test end-to-end carefully, because:\\n- multiple agents currently assume fixed `/tmp/...` paths\\n- publisher/wp steps may have hidden dependencies\\n- one missed path would break the run\\n\\nSo my POV: **phased migration is much safer**.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# What specifically needs replacing\\n\\n## Research step\\nCurrent risk:\\n- writes to global `/tmp/researcher-raw.txt`\\n\\nBetter:\\n- write to `RUN_DIR/research/raw.json`\\n- validate into `RUN_DIR/research/validated.json`\\n\\n## Writer step\\nCurrent risk:\\n- writes to global `/tmp/crypto-article-raw.md`\\n\\nBetter:\\n- write to `RUN_DIR/article/raw.md`\\n- sanitize/validate into `RUN_DIR/article/final.md`\\n\\n## Image/chart step\\nCurrent status:\\n- partly safer already via symlinked current-run targets\\n\\nBetter:\\n- generate directly into `RUN_DIR/media/...`\\n\\n## DOCX/export step\\nCurrent risk:\\n- `/tmp/crypto-article.docx` is global\\n\\nBetter:\\n- build `RUN_DIR/article/article.docx`\\n\\n## Publish step\\nCurrent risk:\\n- may publish whichever global file exists\\n\\nBetter:\\n- publish exact file path from manifest\\n\\n---\\n\\n# The old system I would replace first\\nIf I had to prioritize conceptually, I’d replace these first:\\n\\n1. **global raw writer file**\\n   - biggest stale-article risk\\n\\n2. **global researcher raw file**\\n   - can confuse retries and validation\\n\\n3. **global docx output**\\n   - can publish stale content even if markdown changed\\n\\nThose three are the main contamination points we actually observed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# My overall POV\\nYour idea is solid. I’d summarize it like this:\\n\\n- **Yes:** isolate each run in its own folder\\n- **Yes:** make downstream read only from that one run bundle\\n- **Yes:** keep legacy paths only as temporary symlinks\\n- **No:** don’t keep shared standalone `/tmp` artifacts as truth\\n\\nIf you want, I can next give you a **very concrete implementation blueprint**:\\n- exact folder tree\\n- exact artifact names\\n- exact read/write contract for each agent\\n- exact migration order with rollback points\\n\\nStill no changes, just the design.\"}],\"api\":\"openai-completions\",\"provider\":\"local-bifrost\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"usage\":{\"input\":2121,\"output\":1699,\"cacheRead\":55808,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":59628,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"stop\",\"timestamp\":1779346707319,\"responseId\":\"chatcmpl-DhreO4yYJWpDIWeIdMLOW0vlSR1e4\"}}\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/agents/orchestrator/sessions/3d69fc49-c0a3-4f8a-ac4e-6e441c7d595d.checkpoint.f701932a-c8a8-48d6-9f48-a64b1009257c.jsonl:193:{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"a8225a78\",\"parentId\":\"bec60e35\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-21T07:05:29.932Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Sender (untrusted metadata):\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"label\\\": \\\"openclaw-control-ui\\\",\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"openclaw-control-ui\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n[Thu 2026-05-21 07:05 UTC] here is my plan to fix you just have to validate or impeovements i can do in this an dif im ready to go my devloper team will do thsi work you jsut give me analysis report of yours \\\"---\\nname: Fix stale article publish\\noverview: Adopt a nested run-bundle per pipeline execution (raw vs validated/final separation, manifest routing table), symlink legacy /tmp paths for compatibility, and enforce sync plus freshness gates before Drive/WordPress. Phased migration Option A; Phases 1–2 ship the stale-article fix.\\ntodos:\\n - id: pipeline-scripts\\n content: Add init_run.sh (nested RUN_DIR tree + manifest artifacts map), sync_article_from_raw.py, verify_artifacts.py, manifest_paths.py, cleanup_run_artifacts.sh\\n status: pending\\n - id: migration-phase1-2\\n content: Phase 1–2 — canonical run-bundle + symlinks; update SOUL/researcher/writer spawn paths; validators read manifest or CRYPTO_RUN_DIR paths\\n status: pending\\n - id: soul-step0-2\\n content: Wire SOUL Step 0 (run bundle folder + symlinks) and Step 2 (mandatory sync + ARTICLE_SYNCED gate); pass RUN_DIR in every spawn message\\n status: pending\\n - id: soul-gates-cleanup\\n content: Add pre-Drive/pre-WP verify_artifacts calls, post-publish cleanup, and session.json wipe before each spawn\\n status: pending\\n - id: anchor-validator\\n content: Promote research URL mismatch from warning to error in validate_anchor_links.py\\n status: pending\\n - id: docs-verify\\n content: Update PIPELINE_ARCHITECTURE + FILE_MANIFEST; run manual split-state and full pipeline verification\\n status: pending\\nisProject: false\\n---\\n\\n# Fix same-article republish (run-bundle model)\\n\\n## Verdict: should we implement the agent’s design?\\n\\n**Yes — this is a good-to-great solution** and we should implement it (phased, not big-bang).\\n\\n| Criterion | Assessment |\\n|-----------|------------|\\n| Fixes observed bug (raw ≠ final ≠ docx) | Yes — isolation + explicit raw/final lineage |\\n| Fits existing code | Yes — Step 0 already uses `crypto-run-*`; ~15 hardcoded `/tmp` refs in SOUL + `publish.sh` |\\n| Fits long-term direction | Yes — [PIPELINE_HARDENING_PLAN_V2](workspace-orchestrator/PIPELINE_HARDENING_PLAN_V2.md) + [memory manifest spec](workspace-orchestrator/memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md) |\\n| Risk | Low if **Option A phased** (symlinks during transition); high if full cutover in one shot |\\n\\n**Implement:** nested run bundle + manifest `artifacts` routing + sync/verify gates + all legacy `/tmp` paths as symlinks only.\\n\\n**Do not implement in v1:** full manifest state machine (resume/approval) — routing table only.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Simple explanation (what went wrong and what we will do)\\n\\n**What you saw:** Research moved on (South Carolina, Fed payments, etc.) but WordPress and Google Drive kept getting the **Canada ATM** article.\\n\\n**Why that happened:** The pipeline uses two different “draft” locations:\\n\\n1. **Raw draft** — `/tmp/crypto-article-raw.md` (where the writer agent saves new text)\\n2. **Canonical draft** — `/tmp/crypto-article.md` (what Drive, pandoc, and WordPress actually read)\\n\\nOnly a **bash step in the orchestrator** copies raw → canonical. The writer updating raw is not enough. Your tests showed raw = new story, canonical = old Canada — so publish always used the old file.\\n\\n**The fix in plain terms (one folder per pipeline run):**\\n\\nEach time you say “run the pipeline,” Nexus creates **one new folder** — that run’s only workspace. Inside it lives **exactly one chosen story** by the end (research → article → docx → image). Example:\\n\\n`/tmp/crypto-run-20260521-120000/`\\n- `research.json` — what Scout found\\n- `researcher-raw.txt` — Scout’s raw output\\n- `article-structure.json` — section/FAQ plan\\n- `article-raw.md` — writer draft\\n- `article.md` — final article (what gets published)\\n- `article.docx` — Drive export\\n- `feature.jpg`, `chart.png`, `manifest.json`\\n\\n**Every step only reads and writes inside that folder** (via symlinks at `/tmp/...` so old scripts still work). No step should “pick whatever file happens to exist in `/tmp` from last week.”\\n\\nThat alone fixes most cross-run confusion. We still add two safety nets because the orchestrator can skip steps:\\n\\n1. **Sync script** — copy raw draft → final `article.md` and verify it matches `research.json`.\\n2. **Verify before publish** — block Drive/WP if the folder’s article doesn’t match research.\\n\\nAfter publish, keep the folder for debugging or delete old runs on a schedule; **never** reuse one folder for a second pipeline run.\\n\\n**Per run, not per story (important nuance):** We isolate by **pipeline execution** (`RUN_ID`), not by “news topic” alone. Scout may try several RSS candidates in one run; retries stay in the same bundle. If two runs pick the same headline on different days, they still get **separate folders** — no cross-run bleed.\\n\\n```mermaid\\nflowchart LR\\n subgraph before [Broken state]\\n R1[raw SC] --> X[skip sanitize]\\n C1[canonical Canada] --> WP1[WordPress]\\n end\\n subgraph after [Fixed state]\\n R2[raw] --> S[sync_and_validate]\\n S --> C2[canonical]\\n C2 --> G[gate matches research]\\n G --> WP2[Drive and WP]\\n end\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Why one folder per pipeline run (agent + your instinct — aligned)\\n\\n**Yes — artifact isolation per run is the single biggest structural fix.** The orchestrator agent’s refinement matches the plan: **one folder per pipeline run, containing exactly one chosen story when research finishes.**\\n\\n| Per-story folder only | Per pipeline run folder (chosen) |\\n|-----------------------|----------------------------------|\\n| Blurs “evaluating candidates” vs “final pick” | Scout can retry candidates **inside same** `RUN_DIR` |\\n| Two runs same topic → ambiguous sharing | Two runs same topic → **two folders**, still isolated |\\n| Harder to audit one execution | `ls RUN_DIR` = full snapshot of that run |\\n\\n| Today (broken) | Proposed (run bundle) |\\n|----------------|----------------------|\\n| Mix of run-scoped + global `/tmp` files | **`RUN_DIR` = source of truth for this execution** |\\n| Downstream “guesses” which file is current | Every step reads/writes **only** via `RUN_DIR` (or symlinks into it) |\\n| research / raw / docx can point to different eras | All artifacts in one bundle **must** agree before publish |\\n\\n**Four rules (must all be true — folder alone is not enough):**\\n\\n1. Every artifact for this run lives in `RUN_DIR`.\\n2. Every step uses only that run’s paths (spawn messages include `RUN_DIR` / `CRYPTO_RUN_DIR`).\\n3. Legacy `/tmp/foo` paths are **symlinks only**, never real stale files.\\n4. No step treats a global `/tmp` file as authoritative if it is not the current run’s symlink target.\\n\\n**What still breaks even with folders:**\\n\\n| Risk | Mitigation in plan |\\n|------|-------------------|\\n| `article-raw.md` updated but `article.md` not (skipped sync) | Mandatory `sync_article_from_raw.py` + `ARTICLE_SYNCED` |\\n| Nexus continues after writer `SUCCESS` without bash | SOUL rule + `verify_artifacts.py` before Drive/WP |\\n| Same topic picked run after run | History / researcher diversity (Phase 2) — separate from stale files |\\n| Sub-agent yields `SUCCESS` without writing files | Session wipe before spawn |\\n\\n**Dangerous global paths today (must become symlinks or run-local only):**\\n\\n- `/tmp/researcher-raw.txt`\\n- `/tmp/crypto-article-raw.md`\\n- `/tmp/article-structure.json`\\n- `/tmp/crypto-article.docx`\\n- `/tmp/crypto-with-image.md`\\n- `/tmp/pipeline-manifest.json` (should live in `RUN_DIR` as `manifest.json`)\\n\\nAlready partly run-scoped but still drifted when globals diverged: `/tmp/research.json`, `/tmp/crypto-article.md` (symlink without clearing sibling globals).\\n\\n```mermaid\\nflowchart TB\\n subgraph runDir [\\\"RUN_DIR per pipeline run\\\"]\\n M[manifest.json]\\n RR[research/raw.json]\\n RV[research/validated.json]\\n AR[article/raw.md]\\n AF[article/final.md]\\n DX[article/article.docx]\\n end\\n Scout --> RR\\n ValResearch --> RV\\n Writer --> AR\\n Sync --> AF\\n Pandoc --> DX\\n WP[WordPress] --> AF\\n Drive[Google Drive] --> DX\\n```\\n\\n**Compatibility:** Legacy `/tmp/research.json`, `/tmp/crypto-article.md`, etc. symlink to **validated/final** paths in the active `RUN_DIR`. `publish.sh` unchanged in Phase 1–2.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Target run-bundle layout (agent blueprint — adopted)\\n\\n```\\n/tmp/crypto-run-<RUN_ID>/\\n manifest.json # routing table + run_id + story + step status\\n .run_started # epoch for freshness checks\\n research/\\n raw.json # Scout output (was researcher-raw.txt)\\n validated.json # Step 1 validator output (was /tmp/research.json)\\n structure.json # pick_article_structure (was article-structure.json)\\n article/\\n raw.md # Quill output (was crypto-article-raw.md)\\n final.md # sync + sanitize (was crypto-article.md)\\n with-image.md # Step 4 embed\\n article.docx # pandoc output (was global docx)\\n media/\\n feature.jpg\\n chart.png\\n publish/\\n google-drive.json # optional: Drive upload result\\n wordpress.json # wp-result.json\\n```\\n\\n**Lineage rule (fixes raw/final/docx drift):**\\n\\n| Stage | Reads | Writes |\\n|-------|-------|--------|\\n| Scout | RSS | `research/raw.json` |\\n| Step 1 validator | `research/raw.json` | `research/validated.json` |\\n| pick_structure | `research/validated.json` | `research/structure.json` |\\n| Quill | `validated.json` + `structure.json` | `article/raw.md` |\\n| sync + validate | `article/raw.md` + `validated.json` | `article/final.md` |\\n| pandoc | `article/with-image.md` or `final.md` | `article/article.docx` |\\n| WP / Drive | manifest `article_final` / `docx` | `publish/*.json` |\\n\\nWriter **never** reads `article/final.md`; publisher **never** reads `article/raw.md`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phased migration (Option A — recommended)\\n\\n### Phase 1 — Introduce bundle + symlinks (fixes stale publish)\\n- `init_run.sh` creates nested tree + empty placeholders\\n- Write canonical files only under `RUN_DIR`\\n- Symlink **all** legacy globals into bundle (including raw + docx)\\n- `sync_article_from_raw.py` + `verify_artifacts.py` use manifest paths\\n- SOUL Step 0–2, 4, 6 updated; spawn messages use `$RUN_DIR/...` paths\\n\\n### Phase 2 — Agents and validators use bundle paths explicitly\\n- [workspace-researcher/SOUL.md](workspace-researcher/SOUL.md): write `research/raw.json`\\n- [workspace-writer/SOUL.md](workspace-writer/SOUL.md): read validated + structure; write `article/raw.md`\\n- Orchestrator validators: `--manifest \\\"$RUN_DIR/manifest.json\\\"` or `manifest_paths.py --key article_final`\\n- [publish.sh](workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh): optional `ARTICLE_PATH` / `IMAGE_PATH` env from manifest (default stays symlinks)\\n\\n### Phase 3 — Internal logic stops assuming globals\\n- Scripts resolve paths via manifest first; `/tmp/foo` only via symlink\\n- `update_manifest.py` after each step (paths + `story.headline` + step status)\\n\\n### Phase 4 — Remove legacy symlinks (later)\\n- Only after e2e proof; `publish.sh` reads manifest directly\\n\\n**Rollback:** Keep previous flat `crypto-run-*` dirs on disk; Phase 1 only changes active run behavior.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Manifest as routing table (minimal v1)\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n \\\"run_id\\\": \\\"20260521-055616\\\",\\n \\\"run_dir\\\": \\\"/tmp/crypto-run-20260521-055616\\\",\\n \\\"created_at\\\": \\\"2026-05-21T05:56:16Z\\\",\\n \\\"current_step\\\": \\\"write\\\",\\n \\\"story\\\": { \\\"story_id\\\": \\\"...\\\", \\\"headline\\\": \\\"...\\\" },\\n \\\"artifacts\\\": {\\n \\\"research_raw\\\": \\\".../research/raw.json\\\",\\n \\\"research_validated\\\": \\\".../research/validated.json\\\",\\n \\\"article_structure\\\": \\\".../research/structure.json\\\",\\n \\\"article_raw\\\": \\\".../article/raw.md\\\",\\n \\\"article_final\\\": \\\".../article/final.md\\\",\\n \\\"article_with_image\\\": \\\".../article/with-image.md\\\",\\n \\\"docx\\\": \\\".../article/article.docx\\\",\\n \\\"feature_image\\\": \\\".../media/feature.jpg\\\",\\n \\\"chart\\\": \\\".../media/chart.png\\\"\\n }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nHelper: `workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/manifest_paths.py --manifest ... --key article_final` for bash/SOUL.\\n\\nAligns with manifest invariants in [memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md](workspace-orchestrator/memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md) (full status machine deferred).\\n\\n### Legacy symlink map (Phase 1)\\n\\n| Legacy path | Symlink target |\\n|-------------|----------------|\\n| `/tmp/research.json` | `research/validated.json` |\\n| `/tmp/researcher-raw.txt` | `research/raw.json` |\\n| `/tmp/article-structure.json` | `research/structure.json` |\\n| `/tmp/crypto-article-raw.md` | `article/raw.md` |\\n| `/tmp/crypto-article.md` | `article/final.md` |\\n| `/tmp/crypto-with-image.md` | `article/with-image.md` |\\n| `/tmp/crypto-article.docx` | `article/article.docx` |\\n| `/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg` | `media/feature.jpg` |\\n| `/tmp/chart.png` | `media/chart.png` |\\n| `/tmp/pipeline-manifest.json` | `manifest.json` |\\n\\n**Never** leave real standalone files at those paths after Step 0.\\n\\n### Freshness guards (agent §7 — included)\\n\\n| Gate | Checks |\\n|------|--------|\\n| Before write | `research_validated` exists; `run_id` matches manifest |\\n| Before sync | `article_raw` mtime ≥ `.run_started` |\\n| After sync | `article_final` mtime ≥ `article_raw`; H1 matches `story.headline` |\\n| Before Drive | `docx` mtime ≥ `article_final`; paths in manifest |\\n| Before WP | `article_final` from manifest; smoke optional |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Root cause (technical, confirmed)\\n\\n| Layer | Finding |\\n|-------|---------|\\n| Writer | Can overwrite [`/tmp/crypto-article-raw.md`](file:///tmp/crypto-article-raw.md) correctly |\\n| Orchestrator Step 2 | Only [`SOUL.md` lines 158–178](workspace-orchestrator/SOUL.md) update canonical; if Nexus yields past this without running bash, canonical stays stale |\\n| Step 4 / Step 6 | Read [`/tmp/crypto-article.md`](file:///tmp/crypto-article.md) and global [`/tmp/crypto-article.docx`](file:///tmp/crypto-article.docx) — never raw |\\n| Step 0 | Symlinks 4 paths into `$RUN_DIR`; leaves global `researcher-raw.txt`, `crypto-article-raw.md`, `article-structure.json`, `docx` untouched |\\n\\nAligns with [PIPELINE_HARDENING_PLAN_V2.md](workspace-orchestrator/PIPELINE_HARDENING_PLAN_V2.md) section 3.3 (shared temp-file reuse).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Implementation plan (Phases 1–2 in first delivery)\\n\\n### 1. New orchestrator scripts\\n\\nAdd under `workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/`:\\n\\n| Script | Role |\\n|--------|------|\\n| `init_run.sh` | Create nested `RUN_DIR`, placeholders, `manifest.json` with `artifacts` map, symlink all legacy `/tmp` paths, export `RUN_DIR` / `CRYPTO_RUN_DIR` |\\n| `manifest_paths.py` | Resolve artifact path by key from manifest (for bash heredocs) |\\n| `validate_research.py` | Parse `research/raw.json` → write `research/validated.json` (extract from SOUL Step 1 inline Python) |\\n| `sync_article_from_raw.py` | `article/raw.md` → `article/final.md` + topic gate vs `research/validated.json` |\\n| `verify_artifacts.py` | Stage gates (pre_write, post_sync, pre_drive, pre_wp) + mtime lineage |\\n| `update_manifest_step.sh` | Set `current_step`, `story`, step timestamps after each success |\\n| `cleanup_run_artifacts.sh` | Drop active `/tmp` symlinks; optional prune old `crypto-run-*` |\\n\\n**Priority contamination fixes (agent order):** global raw writer → global researcher raw → global docx — all become run-local + symlinked in Phase 1.\\n\\n### 2. Expand Step 0 in [workspace-orchestrator/SOUL.md](workspace-orchestrator/SOUL.md)\\n\\nReplace inline mkdir/symlink block with:\\n\\n```bash\\nsource ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/init_run.sh\\n# sets RUN_ID, RUN_DIR, CRYPTO_RUN_DIR; creates full bundle + symlinks\\n```\\n\\nRule for Nexus: **“This pipeline run = this `RUN_DIR` only. Never read/write handoff files outside it except via symlinks created in Step 0.”**\\n\\n`init_run.sh` symlinks **every** legacy `/tmp` handoff path into `$RUN_DIR` (see table in §0). No global handoff file remains a real file — only symlinks.\\n\\n### 3. Harden Step 2 in SOUL.md\\n\\nAfter writer `SUCCESS`, **require** this sequence (no skipping):\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/sync_article_from_raw.py \\\\\\n --manifest \\\"$RUN_DIR/manifest.json\\\"\\n# reads article_raw, article_final, research_validated from manifest\\n```\\n\\nThen existing validators (word count, structure, anchors).\\n\\n**SOUL wording change:** Add explicit rule: *“You MUST run `sync_article_from_raw.py` and see `ARTICLE_SYNCED` before Step 3. If you only see writer SUCCESS, the pipeline is NOT done with Step 2.”*\\n\\nKeep inline sanitize logic in script (PTY strip, thinking blocks) — SOUL references script only to avoid duplicate Python.\\n\\n### 4. Gates before publish paths\\n\\n**Before Step 4 (Drive):**\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/verify_artifacts.py \\\\\\n --stage pre_drive --run-dir \\\"$RUN_DIR\\\"\\n```\\n\\n**Before Step 6 (WordPress):** same with `--stage pre_wp`.\\n\\nOn failure: stop pipeline, tell user canonical/raw/research mismatch (show H1 vs headline).\\n\\n### 5. Tighten writer anchor validation\\n\\nIn [`workspace-writer/skills/validate_anchor_links.py`](workspace-writer/skills/validate_anchor_links.py):\\n\\n- When `research.json` is passed, promote “source link not in research source_urls” from **warning** to **error** (at least one body source must match a research URL).\\n\\nOrchestrator already calls this after sync; failures trigger existing repair retry.\\n\\n### 6. Post-publish cleanup\\n\\nIn SOUL after Step 6 success (and optionally after Step 4 Drive-only completion):\\n\\n```bash\\nbash ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/cleanup_run_artifacts.sh --run-dir \\\"$RUN_DIR\\\"\\n```\\n\\nDoes **not** delete `$RUN_DIR` by default (audit trail); removes global symlinks’ stale targets only if documented.\\n\\n### 7. Session wipe (prevent false SUCCESS)\\n\\nPer [PIPELINE_DOCS/03_AGENT_PROFILES.md](PIPELINE_DOCS/03_AGENT_PROFILES.md), add to SOUL before **each** `sessions_spawn`:\\n\\n```bash\\nrm -f ~/.openclaw/agents/<agent>/sessions/sessions.json\\n```\\n\\nFor: `researcher`, `writer`, `creator`, `chart-generator`, `publisher`, `wp-publisher`.\\n\\n### 8. Secondary: history and researcher diversity (Phase 2, same PR or follow-up)\\n\\n- **History on Drive success:** After Step 4, if `/tmp/openclaw_active_url.txt` exists, call `article_history.sh add` (mirror [publish.sh Phase 5](workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh)) so skipping WP still records the URL.\\n- **Researcher:** In [workspace-researcher/SOUL.md](workspace-researcher/SOUL.md), reinforce: on `EXISTS`, pick next candidate; orchestrator Step 1 validator can grep researcher output log for `NOT_FOUND` / require `story_id` in manifest.\\n- **Parallel tests:** Document in SOUL — never spawn multiple researchers to same `researcher-raw.txt` path.\\n\\n### 9. Docs touch-up\\n\\n- [PIPELINE_ARCHITECTURE.md](PIPELINE_ARCHITECTURE.md) — handoff table: all artifacts run-scoped + sync step\\n- [PIPELINE_DOCS/05_FILE_MANIFEST.md](PIPELINE_DOCS/05_FILE_MANIFEST.md) — list new scripts and cleanup behavior\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Verification plan (manual)\\n\\n1. **Split-state repro:** Set raw=SC, canonical=Canada; run `sync_article_from_raw.py` → canonical becomes SC; `verify_artifacts.py` passes.\\n2. **Full pipeline:** Run orchestrator; confirm logs contain `ARTICLE_SYNCED` and `ARTIFACTS_OK` before Drive.\\n3. **Mismatch guard:** Deliberately skip sync; `verify_artifacts.py` must exit non-zero and pipeline must not upload.\\n4. **Publish content:** WP post H1/slug match `research.json` `primary_headline`, not Canada slug.\\n5. **Regression:** Writer-only test still works when followed by sync script.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Out of scope (for this plan)\\n\\n- Tweet URL rescue, variable structure changes (already shipped)\\n- Full manifest **resume/state machine** (approval, `active_process`, auto-continue) — routing table only\\n- Phase 4 legacy symlink removal\\n- Automated researcher “pick 2nd story” script (optional follow-up)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Files to change (summary)\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| [workspace-orchestrator/SOUL.md](workspace-orchestrator/SOUL.md) | Run bundle paths, manifest-driven validators, sync/verify gates, session wipe |\\n| `workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/*` | init, manifest_paths, validate_research, sync, verify, update_manifest, cleanup |\\n| [workspace-researcher/SOUL.md](workspace-researcher/SOUL.md) | Write `$RUN_DIR/research/raw.json` (spawn provides path) |\\n| [workspace-writer/SOUL.md](workspace-writer/SOUL.md) | Read validated + structure; write `article/raw.md` |\\n| [workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh](workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh) | Optional env overrides from manifest (Phase 2) |\\n| [workspace-writer/skills/validate_anchor_links.py](workspace-writer/skills/validate_anchor_links.py) | Mismatch → error |\\n| [PIPELINE_ARCHITECTURE.md](PIPELINE_ARCHITECTURE.md), [PIPELINE_DOCS/05_FILE_MANIFEST.md](PIPELINE_DOCS/05_FILE_MANIFEST.md) | Run-bundle layout + migration phases |\\n\\nNo changes to `openclaw.json` or agent list required.\\n\\\"\"}],\"timestamp\":1779347129926}}\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/agents/orchestrator/sessions/3d69fc49-c0a3-4f8a-ac4e-6e441c7d595d.checkpoint.f701932a-c8a8-48d6-9f48-a64b1009257c.jsonl-194-{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"371134b9\",\"parentId\":\"a8225a78\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-21T07:07:29.617Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"This is a **strong plan**. I’d call it **ready with a few important adjustments** before your dev team implements it.\\n\\n## Executive verdict\\n\\n**Go / implement** with **Option A phased migration**.  \\nYour plan addresses the real bug we observed:\\n\\n- `raw.md` = new story\\n- `article.md` = old story\\n- `docx` = old story\\n\\nSo the core fix, **run-bundle + manifest routing + sync/freshness gates**, is exactly the right direction.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# What’s especially good in your plan\\n\\n## 1. You identified the real failure mode correctly\\nYour explanation of:\\n\\n- writer updates raw draft\\n- orchestrator sync step is separate\\n- publishers read canonical/final paths, not raw\\n\\n…matches what we saw in testing.\\n\\nThat means the plan is grounded in the actual bug, not just theory.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. `RUN_DIR` as the source of truth is the right model\\nThis is the biggest win.\\n\\nA single run bundle containing:\\n\\n- research raw\\n- research validated\\n- article raw\\n- article final\\n- docx\\n- media\\n- publish outputs\\n\\n…is the cleanest way to prevent cross-run bleed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Raw vs final separation is exactly right\\nThis is important and you handled it well.\\n\\nYou’re not just moving files into folders, you’re defining **lineage**:\\n\\n- Scout writes raw\\n- validator writes validated\\n- writer writes raw\\n- sync writes final\\n- export writes docx\\n- publish reads final/docx only\\n\\nThat is the correct abstraction.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Symlinked legacy paths for migration is the right implementation strategy\\nThis is the safest way to ship the stale-article fix without breaking everything at once.\\n\\nI agree with your judgment:\\n\\n- phased = low risk\\n- big-bang = unnecessary risk\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. `verify_artifacts.py` gates before Drive/WP are essential\\nGood call.\\n\\nThis is the safety net that prevents “writer said SUCCESS, but canonical/docx still old” from escaping into publishing.\\n\\nThat’s one of the highest-value parts of the whole plan.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# My recommended improvements\\n\\nThese are the main refinements I’d suggest before you hand this to the dev team.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## A. Do **not** cleanup after Step 4 if WordPress may still happen\\nThis is the biggest adjustment I’d make.\\n\\nYou wrote:\\n\\n> Add pre-Drive/pre-WP verify_artifacts calls, post-publish cleanup\\n\\nThat’s good in principle, but cleanup timing matters.\\n\\n### Why\\nAfter Step 4, the system pauses and asks the user:\\n\\n- yes → publish to WP\\n- no → stop\\n\\nSo if you clean too early after Drive upload, you can accidentally remove artifacts still needed for Step 6.\\n\\n### Recommendation\\nCleanup should happen only after one of these:\\n1. user says **no**\\n2. WordPress publish completes\\n3. pipeline fails terminally and artifacts are intentionally archived or purged\\n\\n### My suggestion\\nTreat `RUN_DIR` as **live and preserved** through the confirmation gate.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## B. Be careful with “wipe sessions.json before each spawn”\\nThis is the one part I’m least confident about.\\n\\nI understand why it’s in the plan: prevent false “SUCCESS” or stale agent state.\\n\\nBut from a systems perspective, it’s a bit blunt.\\n\\n### Risks\\n- it may interfere with valid agent session behavior\\n- it may create side effects outside this specific run\\n- it may become a hidden destructive dependency\\n- if two things ever run close together, it could create weird races\\n\\n### Better primary defense\\nI’d rather rely on:\\n- isolated subagent runs\\n- explicit per-run output paths\\n- freshness checks\\n- required file existence/mtime/content validation\\n\\n### My recommendation\\nMake session wipe **optional / last resort**, not part of the core fix.\\n\\nIf the team keeps it, I’d ask them to explicitly confirm:\\n- what file is being wiped\\n- whether it’s safe across concurrent runs\\n- whether it’s needed after run-bundle isolation is in place\\n\\n**My preference:** solve this with path isolation and verification first, not session-file deletion.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## C. Make file writes atomic\\nThis is an important implementation detail that your plan doesn’t state explicitly.\\n\\n### Why it matters\\nEven with `RUN_DIR`, you can still get half-written or partially updated files if:\\n- a process exits mid-write\\n- a validator reads during write\\n- a subagent writes and then crashes\\n\\n### Recommendation\\nFor critical artifacts, use:\\n- write to temp file in same directory\\n- rename into place only when complete\\n\\nEspecially for:\\n- `research/raw.json`\\n- `research/validated.json`\\n- `article/raw.md`\\n- `article/final.md`\\n- `article/article.docx`\\n- `manifest.json`\\n\\nThis will make the bundle model much more reliable.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## D. Strengthen the coherence check beyond just H1/headline\\nYour `verify_artifacts` concept is good, but I’d make the content match test a bit stronger.\\n\\n### Why\\nA matching H1 alone is helpful, but not always enough:\\n- article body could still be stale or mixed\\n- title may be rewritten while body stays old\\n- slug/docx could still be out of sync\\n\\n### Recommendation\\nBefore Drive/WP, verify at least:\\n- `article_final` exists and is fresh\\n- `docx` exists and is newer than `article_final`\\n- final article H1 aligns with `research_validated.primary_headline`\\n- at least one/two URLs in article sources or body are from current `research_validated.source_urls`\\n- optional: slug/title in DOCX or publish metadata aligns with current story\\n\\nThis catches “same title, wrong body” cases better.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## E. Promote more than anchor mismatch to hard failure\\nYour idea to make anchor URL mismatch an error is good. I’d support it.\\n\\nI’d also consider hard-failing if:\\n- `article_final` references source URLs not present in current validated research\\n- `docx` is older than final markdown\\n- `publish.sh` source path is not the manifest path for this run\\n\\nThat gives you a consistent “no stale lineage passes publish” rule.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## F. Prefer manifest lookup over environment spread where possible\\nUsing `RUN_DIR` / `CRYPTO_RUN_DIR` is fine, but I’d still push the team to make the **manifest the authority**.\\n\\n### Good pattern\\n- env var tells scripts where the manifest is\\n- scripts read actual artifact paths from manifest\\n- downstream steps don’t guess paths\\n\\nThat keeps the system more future-proof if paths evolve later.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## G. Consider an `active-run` pointer in addition to symlinks\\nNot mandatory, but useful.\\n\\nExample:\\n- `/tmp/crypto-active-run` contains the active `RUN_DIR`\\n- legacy symlinks still exist\\n\\n### Why it helps\\nWhen debugging, tooling can quickly answer:\\n- what run is active?\\n- which bundle owns current symlinks?\\n- is this file really from the active run?\\n\\nNot required for the fix, but operationally nice.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Things I would explicitly approve as-is\\n\\nThese are good and I’d keep them.\\n\\n- **Option A phased migration**\\n- nested run bundle\\n- manifest artifacts map\\n- raw vs validated/final separation\\n- `sync_article_from_raw.py`\\n- `verify_artifacts.py`\\n- all legacy `/tmp` paths become symlinks only\\n- Step 2 mandatory sync gate\\n- pre-Drive and pre-WP verify gates\\n- anchor validator mismatch promoted to error\\n- docs updates + manual split-state verification\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Things I would change before implementation\\n\\n## 1. Cleanup timing\\nChange from:\\n- “cleanup after Step 4 or Step 6”\\n\\nTo:\\n- “cleanup only after explicit terminal state: user says no, or WP publish completes, or terminal failure/archive policy”\\n\\n## 2. Session wipe\\nChange from:\\n- “wipe before each spawn” as standard behavior\\n\\nTo:\\n- “only if proven necessary after path isolation; otherwise avoid”\\n\\n## 3. Add atomic-write requirement\\nAdd this explicitly to implementation notes.\\n\\n## 4. Strengthen verify rules\\nMake verification check:\\n- freshness\\n- lineage\\n- source coherence\\n- manifest path ownership\\n\\nNot just H1 alignment.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Readiness assessment\\n\\n## Is the plan conceptually correct?\\n**Yes.**\\n\\n## Does it fix the stale publish bug?\\n**Yes, very likely.**\\n\\n## Is it safe to hand to devs now?\\n**Yes, with the refinements above.**\\n\\n## My confidence\\n**High** that Phases 1–2 will fix the repeated stale-article publish issue if implemented carefully.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# My final recommendation to your dev team\\n\\nI’d summarize my review like this:\\n\\n### Approved direction\\n- adopt run-bundle model\\n- manifest as routing table\\n- raw/final lineage\\n- legacy symlink compatibility\\n- publish gates before Drive/WP\\n\\n### Required tweaks\\n- do not cleanup before WP decision is resolved\\n- avoid making session-file wipe a core dependency unless proven necessary\\n- use atomic writes for all critical artifacts\\n- verify body/source lineage, not only H1 freshness\\n\\n---\\n\\nIf you want, I can turn your draft into a **dev-facing review memo** with:\\n- **Approved**\\n- **Needs change**\\n- **Optional improvements**\\n- **Go / no-go**\\n\\nStill analysis only, no edits.\"}],\"api\":\"openai-completions\",\"provider\":\"local-bifrost\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"usage\":{\"input\":64939,\"output\":2482,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":67421,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"stop\",\"timestamp\":1779347129938,\"responseId\":\"chatcmpl-Dhrlm6o26vwYXnuGdp3aich7F5S2J\"}}\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/agents/orchestrator/sessions/3d69fc49-c0a3-4f8a-ac4e-6e441c7d595d.checkpoint.f701932a-c8a8-48d6-9f48-a64b1009257c.jsonl-195-{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"dbbd8224\",\"parentId\":\"371134b9\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-21T07:10:27.016Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Sender (untrusted metadata):\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"label\\\": \\\"openclaw-control-ui\\\",\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"openclaw-control-ui\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n[Thu 2026-05-21 07:10 UTC] something left or truncated would you like to continue form where you left\"}],\"timestamp\":1779347427011}}\n--\n/home/bhard/.