\":151,\"endLine\":181,\"score\":1,\"textScore\":0.8158183970176884,\"snippet\":\"assistant: Got it — publishing the draft to WordPress now, then I’ll smoke-check the preview before I report back.\\nuser: System (untrusted): [2026-05-18 10:13:08 UTC] Exec completed (tidal-me, code 0) :: [2KWP_DRAFT_URL=https://slateblue-reindeer-775070.hostingersite.com/?p=93 SMOKE_WARN: Could not fetch: HTTP Error 403: Forbidden\\n\\nConversation info (untrusted metadata):\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"chat_id\\\": \\\"telegram:5691449303\\\",\\n  \\\"message_id\\\": \\\"503\\\",\\n  \\\"sender_id\\\": \\\"5691449303\\\",\\n  \\\"sender\\\": \\\"Sawan bhardwaj\\\",\\n  \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"Mon 2026-05-18 10:16 UTC\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\nSender (untrusted metadata):\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"label\\\": \\\"Sawan bhardwaj (5691449303)\\\",\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"5691449303\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"Sawan bhardwaj\\\",\\n  \\\"username\\\": \\\"her\\n\\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-news-pipeline.md#L151-L181\",\"source\":\"memory\",\"citation\":\"memory/2026-05-18-news-pipeline.md#L151-L181\",\"corpus\":\"memory\"}],\"provider\":\"none\",\"citations\":\"auto\",\"debug\":{\"backend\":\"builtin\",\"effectiveMode\":\"n/a\",\"searchMs\":23,\"hits\":3}},\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1779347438310}}\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/agents/orchestrator/sessions/3d69fc49-c0a3-4f8a-ac4e-6e441c7d595d.checkpoint.f701932a-c8a8-48d6-9f48-a64b1009257c.jsonl-198-{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"6e1d83f3\",\"parentId\":\"3f2ee335\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-21T07:11:12.625Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Yes — a little. The core verdict was complete, but here’s the clean finish from where I left off.\\n\\n## Final go / no-go\\n**Go**, with **4 required tweaks** before implementation:\\n\\n1. **Do not cleanup after Step 4** if WordPress may still happen  \\n2. **Do not rely on session-file wiping** as a core fix unless proven necessary  \\n3. **Use atomic writes** for all critical artifacts  \\n4. **Strengthen verification** beyond H1/title freshness\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The last missing piece: implementation risk ranking\\n\\n### Highest-value changes\\nThese are the ones most likely to fix the bug quickly:\\n\\n1. **Make all legacy `/tmp` handoff paths symlinks into `RUN_DIR`**\\n2. **Add mandatory raw → final sync step**\\n3. **Add pre-Drive and pre-WP artifact verification**\\n4. **Move docx into run bundle and publish only manifest-routed files**\\n\\nIf they only ship those carefully, I’d already expect a major improvement.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Medium-priority improvements\\nThese make the system more robust after the stale publish bug is fixed:\\n\\n- stricter anchor/source validation\\n- manifest path helper tooling\\n- docs refresh\\n- post-run cleanup\\n- richer per-step manifest updates\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Lowest-priority / caution area\\nThese are the parts I would *not* make central to v1 of the fix:\\n\\n- full manifest state machine / resume system\\n- aggressive session wiping before each spawn\\n- removing legacy symlinks entirely\\n- researcher diversity/history logic\\n\\nThose can come later.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## My final review in one sentence\\nYour plan is **architecturally sound, grounded in the actual failure we observed, and ready for the dev team** once they tighten cleanup timing, avoid overusing session wipes, and add atomic-write + stronger verification rules.\\n\\nIf you want, I can now turn this into a **very compact dev handoff checklist** with:\\n- **Approved**\\n- **Must change**\\n- **Nice to have**\\n- **Ship recommendation**\"}],\"api\":\"openai-completions\",\"provider\":\"local-bifrost\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"usage\":{\"input\":1500,\"output\":422,\"cacheRead\":66816,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":68738,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"stop\",\"timestamp\":1779347438313,\"responseId\":\"chatcmpl-DhrqB4eiuUQpY8NYgfkYJFvPblnAF\"}}\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/agents/orchestrator/sessions/3d69fc49-c0a3-4f8a-ac4e-6e441c7d595d.checkpoint.f701932a-c8a8-48d6-9f48-a64b1009257c.jsonl:199:{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"3d657487\",\"parentId\":\"6e1d83f3\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-21T07:18:47.898Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Sender (untrusted metadata):\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"label\\\": \\\"openclaw-control-ui\\\",\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"openclaw-control-ui\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n[Thu 2026-05-21 07:18 UTC] okay one more thing what about this now then \\\"---\\nname: Fix stale article publish\\noverview: Fix same-article republish by treating each pipeline execution as a self-contained run-bundle with raw/final lineage, manifest routing, atomic writes, and strong coherence gates before Drive/WordPress. Phased migration so nothing breaks.\\ntodos:\\n - id: pipeline-scripts\\n content: \\\"Add 7 scripts under workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/: init_run.sh, manifest_paths.py, validate_research.py, sync_article_from_raw.py (atomic writes), verify_artifacts.py (coherence+lineage), update_manifest_step.sh, cleanup_run_artifacts.sh\\\"\\n status: pending\\n - id: soul-step0-2\\n content: \\\"SOUL Step 0: init_run.sh (nested bundle + all symlinks + active-run pointer). Step 2: mandatory sync gate with ARTICLE_SYNCED required; spawn messages use $RUN_DIR explicit paths\\\"\\n status: pending\\n - id: soul-gates-verify\\n content: \\\"SOUL: pre-Drive coherence gate (lineage+source URLs), pre-WP coherence gate (manifest path), update_manifest_step after each success\\\"\\n status: pending\\n - id: cleanup-timing\\n content: \\\"Cleanup only on terminal state: user says NO to WP, WP publish completes, or pipeline fatal failure. RUN_DIR stays live through Drive→WP gate.\\\"\\n status: pending\\n - id: anchor-validator\\n content: Promote research URL mismatch from warning to error in validate_anchor_links.py; verify_artifacts checks docx mtime > article/final.md\\n status: pending\\n - id: docs-verify\\n content: Update PIPELINE_ARCHITECTURE + FILE_MANIFEST; run split-state repro test, full pipeline test, mismatch guard test\\n status: pending\\nisProject: false\\n---\\n\\n# Fix same-article republish (run-bundle model — final plan)\\n\\n## Final verdict\\n\\n**Go — implement Phases 1–2 with 4 required adjustments incorporated.**\\n\\n| Criterion | Assessment |\\n|-----------|------------|\\n| Fixes observed bug (raw ≠ final ≠ docx) | Yes — isolation + lineage + coherence gates |\\n| Fits existing code | Yes — Step 0 already uses `crypto-run-*`; ~15 `/tmp` refs become symlinks |\\n| Fits long-term direction | Yes — [PIPELINE_HARDENING_PLAN_V2](workspace-orchestrator/PIPELINE_HARDENING_PLAN_V2.md) + manifest spec in memory |\\n| Safe | Yes — phased; all legacy `/tmp` paths stay as symlinks, nothing changes for `publish.sh` until Phase 2 |\\n\\n**4 required adjustments (from final review):**\\n\\n| # | What | Changed from earlier draft |\\n|---|------|--------------------------|\\n| 1 | **Cleanup timing** | Only on terminal state (user NO / WP done / fatal) — not after Drive alone |\\n| 2 | **Session wipe removed** | Path isolation + mtime + required `ARTICLE_SYNCED` are the primary defence |\\n| 3 | **Atomic writes** | All critical artifact writes use temp-file-then-rename |\\n| 4 | **Stronger verify** | Freshness + lineage (docx mtime ≥ final.md) + source URL coherence, not just H1 |\\n\\n**Not in v1:** full manifest state machine (resume/approval), Phase 4 symlink removal, researcher diversity.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Simple explanation (what went wrong, what we fix)\\n\\n**What you saw:** Research moved on (South Carolina, Fed payments) but WordPress and Google Drive kept getting **Canada ATM** — for 6+ runs.\\n\\n**Why:** Two separate file locations existed for \\\"the article\\\":\\n\\n- `crypto-article-raw.md` — where Writer saves a new draft\\n- `crypto-article.md` — what Drive, pandoc, and WordPress actually read\\n\\nOnly one specific bash block in the orchestrator copies raw → canonical. Writer updating raw is not enough. Your live tests confirmed: raw = South Carolina, canonical = old Canada, docx = old Canada.\\n\\n**The fix — one folder per pipeline run:**\\n\\n```\\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260521-120000/ ← one run, one story\\n manifest.json\\n research/\\n raw.json ← Scout's output\\n validated.json ← what Writer reads\\n structure.json ← what Writer reads\\n article/\\n raw.md ← Writer's draft\\n final.md ← what Drive/WP publish\\n with-image.md\\n article.docx\\n media/\\n feature.jpg\\n chart.png\\n publish/\\n google-drive.json\\n wordpress.json\\n```\\n\\nEvery step reads and writes **only** inside that folder. Legacy `/tmp/research.json`, `/tmp/crypto-article.md`, etc. become **symlinks** pointing into the active run folder — so `publish.sh` and old scripts keep working with no changes.\\n\\nTwo safety nets inside the folder:\\n\\n1. **Sync script** — copies raw → final and verifies article topic matches research.\\n2. **Coherence gates** — block Drive and WordPress if article/docx lineage is broken.\\n\\n```mermaid\\nflowchart TB\\n subgraph runDir [\\\"RUN_DIR — one pipeline run\\\"]\\n M[manifest.json]\\n RR[\\\"research/raw.json\\\"]\\n RV[\\\"research/validated.json\\\"]\\n AR[\\\"article/raw.md\\\"]\\n AF[\\\"article/final.md\\\"]\\n DX[\\\"article/article.docx\\\"]\\n end\\n Scout --> RR\\n ValResearch --> RV\\n Writer --> AR\\n Sync --> AF\\n Pandoc --> DX\\n WP[WordPress] --> AF\\n Drive[Google Drive] --> DX\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Target run-bundle layout\\n\\n```\\n/tmp/crypto-run-<RUN_ID>/\\n manifest.json # routing table + run_id + story + current_step\\n .run_started # epoch timestamp written at Step 0\\n research/\\n raw.json # Scout output (was /tmp/researcher-raw.txt)\\n validated.json # Step 1 output (was /tmp/research.json)\\n structure.json # pick_article_structure (was /tmp/article-structure.json)\\n article/\\n raw.md # Quill output (was /tmp/crypto-article-raw.md)\\n final.md # sync output (was /tmp/crypto-article.md)\\n with-image.md # Step 4 embed (was /tmp/crypto-with-image.md)\\n article.docx # pandoc output (was /tmp/crypto-article.docx)\\n media/\\n feature.jpg # (was /tmp/crypto-feature.jpg)\\n chart.png # (was /tmp/chart.png)\\n publish/\\n google-drive.json\\n wordpress.json # (was /tmp/wp-result.json)\\n```\\n\\n**Lineage rule — each stage reads only its designated input:**\\n\\n| Stage | Reads | Writes |\\n|-------|-------|--------|\\n| Scout | RSS feeds | `research/raw.json` |\\n| Step 1 validator | `research/raw.json` | `research/validated.json` |\\n| pick_structure | `research/validated.json` | `research/structure.json` |\\n| Quill (Writer) | `validated.json` + `structure.json` | `article/raw.md` |\\n| sync + sanitize | `article/raw.md` + `validated.json` | `article/final.md` |\\n| pandoc | `article/with-image.md` | `article/article.docx` |\\n| WP / Drive | manifest `article_final` / `docx` | `publish/*.json` |\\n\\nWriter **never** reads `article/final.md`. Publisher **never** reads `article/raw.md`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Legacy symlink map (Phase 1 — all in `init_run.sh`)\\n\\n| Legacy `/tmp` path | Symlink target in `RUN_DIR` |\\n|--------------------|-----------------------------|\\n| `/tmp/research.json` | `research/validated.json` |\\n| `/tmp/researcher-raw.txt` | `research/raw.json` |\\n| `/tmp/article-structure.json` | `research/structure.json` |\\n| `/tmp/crypto-article-raw.md` | `article/raw.md` |\\n| `/tmp/crypto-article.md` | `article/final.md` |\\n| `/tmp/crypto-with-image.md` | `article/with-image.md` |\\n| `/tmp/crypto-article.docx` | `article/article.docx` |\\n| `/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg` | `media/feature.jpg` |\\n| `/tmp/chart.png` | `media/chart.png` |\\n| `/tmp/pipeline-manifest.json` | `manifest.json` |\\n| `/tmp/wp-result.json` | `publish/wordpress.json` |\\n\\n**Never leave a real standalone file at these paths after Step 0.** `init_run.sh` wipes any stale real file and places only symlinks.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Manifest as routing table (minimal v1)\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n \\\"run_id\\\": \\\"20260521-055616\\\",\\n \\\"run_dir\\\": \\\"/tmp/crypto-run-20260521-055616\\\",\\n \\\"created_at\\\": \\\"2026-05-21T05:56:16Z\\\",\\n \\\"current_step\\\": \\\"write\\\",\\n \\\"story\\\": { \\\"story_id\\\": \\\"...\\\", \\\"headline\\\": \\\"...\\\" },\\n \\\"artifacts\\\": {\\n \\\"research_raw\\\": \\\".../research/raw.json\\\",\\n \\\"research_validated\\\": \\\".../research/validated.json\\\",\\n \\\"article_structure\\\": \\\".../research/structure.json\\\",\\n \\\"article_raw\\\": \\\".../article/raw.md\\\",\\n \\\"article_final\\\": \\\".../article/final.md\\\",\\n \\\"article_with_image\\\": \\\".../article/with-image.md\\\",\\n \\\"docx\\\": \\\".../article/article.docx\\\",\\n \\\"feature_image\\\": \\\".../media/feature.jpg\\\",\\n \\\"chart\\\": \\\".../media/chart.png\\\"\\n }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n`manifest_paths.py --manifest \\\"$RUN_DIR/manifest.json\\\" --key article_final` resolves path for bash validators and SOUL heredocs. Aligns with manifest spec in [memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md](workspace-orchestrator/memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Coherence gates — strengthened\\n\\n| Gate | What it checks |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **pre_write** | `research_validated` exists; `run_id` in manifest matches `$RUN_DIR`; file non-empty |\\n| **pre_sync** | `article_raw` mtime ≥ `.run_started`; file non-empty |\\n| **post_sync** | `article_final` mtime ≥ `article_raw`; H1 token-matches `story.headline`; ≥1 body source URL in `research_validated.source_urls` |\\n| **pre_drive** | `docx` mtime ≥ `article_final`; manifest `docx` path is under active `RUN_DIR`; `article_final` non-empty |\\n| **pre_wp** | All pre_drive checks; manifest `article_final` path matches active `RUN_DIR`; H1 + source URL check repeated |\\n\\n\\\"Same title, wrong body\\\" defence: requiring ≥1 source URL match catches title-refreshed-but-body-stale edge case.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Atomic write pattern (required for all critical artifacts)\\n\\nAll scripts that write `research/*.json`, `article/raw.md`, `article/final.md`, `article/article.docx`, `manifest.json` must use:\\n\\n```python\\nimport os, tempfile\\n\\ndef atomic_write(path, content):\\n dir_ = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(path))\\n with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile('w', dir=dir_, delete=False, suffix='.tmp') as f:\\n f.write(content)\\n tmp = f.name\\n os.replace(tmp, path) # atomic rename — never leaves half-written file\\n```\\n\\nBash scripts use `mv --no-clobber` or write to `.tmp` then `mv`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Cleanup timing — terminal state only\\n\\n`cleanup_run_artifacts.sh` is called in exactly three situations:\\n\\n| Situation | SOUL behaviour |\\n|-----------|---------------|\\n| User says **NO** to WordPress | Cleanup then report done |\\n| WordPress publish **succeeds** | Cleanup then report done |\\n| Pipeline **fatal failure** | Cleanup with `--archive` flag; keep `$RUN_DIR` |\\n\\n**`RUN_DIR` stays alive through the Drive → WP confirmation gate.** Drive uploads, orchestrator asks \\\"publish to WP?\\\", user answers — only then cleanup runs.\\n\\nCleanup removes `/tmp` symlinks and `/tmp/crypto-active-run`. Never deletes `$RUN_DIR` itself (kept 7 days for audit; manual or cron prune).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Session wipe — not in core\\n\\nSession wipe is **not** part of the standard flow. The defence against false `SUCCESS` is:\\n\\n1. Spawn message includes explicit `$RUN_DIR/...` paths — agent must write there or mtime check fails.\\n2. `verify_artifacts.py` post_sync checks file exists + mtime ≥ `.run_started`.\\n3. Required `ARTICLE_SYNCED` output in SOUL before Step 3 continues.\\n\\nIf a specific agent is confirmed returning false `SUCCESS` without writing, a targeted `rm -f sessions.json` for that agent only can be added. Not a blanket step.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phased migration\\n\\n### Phase 1 — Run bundle + symlinks (ships stale-article fix)\\n- `init_run.sh` creates nested tree + placeholders + symlinks for all `/tmp` handoff paths\\n- Validators and SOUL read via manifest paths\\n- SOUL Step 0 replaced; Step 2 mandatory sync; pre-Drive/pre-WP gates added\\n- Researcher and Writer spawn messages updated to use `$RUN_DIR/...` explicit paths\\n- Cleanup on terminal state only\\n\\n### Phase 2 — Agents use bundle paths without global fallback\\n- [workspace-researcher/SOUL.md](workspace-researcher/SOUL.md): write `research/raw.json` directly\\n- [workspace-writer/SOUL.md](workspace-writer/SOUL.md): read `research/validated.json` + `research/structure.json`; write `article/raw.md`\\n- Orchestrator validators use `--manifest` flag exclusively\\n- [publish.sh](workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh): `ARTICLE_PATH` / `IMAGE_PATH` from manifest env (default still symlinks)\\n\\n### Phase 3 — Internal logic reads manifest first\\n- All scripts resolve paths via manifest; `/tmp/foo` only via active symlink\\n- `update_manifest_step.sh` called after each step success\\n\\n### Phase 4 (later) — Remove legacy symlinks\\n- After e2e proof; `publish.sh` reads manifest directly; no `/tmp/foo` real files\\n\\n**Rollback:** Old flat `crypto-run-*` dirs untouched; Phase 1 only changes new run behaviour.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Implementation plan (Phases 1–2 in first delivery)\\n\\n### 1. New scripts under `workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/`\\n\\n| Script | Role |\\n|--------|------|\\n| `init_run.sh` | Nested `RUN_DIR`, empty placeholders, `manifest.json`, all legacy symlinks, `/tmp/crypto-active-run`, export `RUN_DIR`/`CRYPTO_RUN_DIR` |\\n| `manifest_paths.py` | `--manifest path --key KEY` → resolve artifact path |\\n| `validate_research.py` | Atomic parse `research/raw.json` → `research/validated.json`; update manifest `story` |\\n| `sync_article_from_raw.py` | Atomic sanitize `article/raw.md` → `article/final.md`; topic + source URL gate |\\n| `verify_artifacts.py` | `--stage pre_write|pre_sync|post_sync|pre_drive|pre_wp` — full coherence checks |\\n| `update_manifest_step.sh` | `--step NAME --status succeeded` — update `current_step` + timestamps |\\n| `cleanup_run_artifacts.sh` | `--run-dir RUN_DIR [--archive]` — remove symlinks + pointer; called on terminal state only |\\n\\n### 2. Step 0 in [workspace-orchestrator/SOUL.md](workspace-orchestrator/SOUL.md)\\n\\nReplace inline mkdir/symlink block with:\\n\\n```bash\\nsource ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/init_run.sh\\n# exports: RUN_ID, RUN_DIR, CRYPTO_RUN_DIR\\n```\\n\\nNew explicit SOUL rule: **\\\"This pipeline run = this `RUN_DIR`. Never read or write handoff files outside it except via symlinks created in Step 0. `$RUN_DIR` is live until terminal state.\\\"**\\n\\n### 3. Step 1 (Research) in SOUL.md\\n\\nResearcher spawn message updated:\\n\\n```\\nFollow your SOUL. Write aggregated JSON to $RUN_DIR/research/raw.json\\n(also at /tmp/researcher-raw.txt via symlink). Yield SUCCESS only.\\n```\\n\\nAfter SUCCESS:\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/validate_research.py \\\\\\n --manifest \\\"$RUN_DIR/manifest.json\\\"\\nbash ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/update_manifest_step.sh \\\\\\n --manifest \\\"$RUN_DIR/manifest.json\\\" --step research --status succeeded\\n```\\n\\n### 4. Step 1.5 (Structure picker) in SOUL.md\\n\\nAfter validate_research:\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-writer/skills/pick_article_structure.py \\\\\\n \\\"$RUN_DIR/research/validated.json\\\" \\\"$RUN_DIR/research/structure.json\\\"\\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/verify_artifacts.py \\\\\\n --stage pre_write --manifest \\\"$RUN_DIR/manifest.json\\\"\\n```\\n\\n### 5. Step 2 (Write) in SOUL.md\\n\\nWriter spawn message:\\n\\n```\\ncat $RUN_DIR/research/validated.json and cat $RUN_DIR/research/structure.json.\\nRead COINOGRAPHY_TEMPLATE.md. Write article to $RUN_DIR/article/raw.md\\n(also at /tmp/crypto-article-raw.md via symlink). Yield SUCCESS only.\\n```\\n\\nAfter SUCCESS, **required before Step 3** (SOUL explicit rule):\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/verify_artifacts.py \\\\\\n --stage pre_sync --manifest \\\"$RUN_DIR/manifest.json\\\"\\n\\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/sync_article_from_raw.py \\\\\\n --manifest \\\"$RUN_DIR/manifest.json\\\"\\n# Must print ARTICLE_SYNCED — if not, stop and report\\n\\n# existing validators (word count, structure counts, anchor links)\\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-writer/skills/validate_article_structure.py ...\\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-writer/skills/validate_anchor_links.py ...\\n\\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/verify_artifacts.py \\\\\\n --stage post_sync --manifest \\\"$RUN_DIR/manifest.json\\\"\\n```\\n\\nSOUL rule: **\\\"You MUST see `ARTICLE_SYNCED` and `post_sync ARTIFACTS_OK` before Step 3. Writer SUCCESS alone is not sufficient.\\\"**\\n\\n### 6. Step 4 (Drive) in SOUL.md\\n\\nBefore pandoc:\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/verify_artifacts.py \\\\\\n --stage pre_drive --manifest \\\"$RUN_DIR/manifest.json\\\"\\n```\\n\\npandoc uses `$RUN_DIR/article/with-image.md` → `$RUN_DIR/article/article.docx`.\\n\\nAfter Drive success:\\n\\n```bash\\nbash ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/update_manifest_step.sh \\\\\\n --manifest \\\"$RUN_DIR/manifest.json\\\" --step drive --status succeeded\\n```\\n\\n### 7. Step 6 (WordPress) in SOUL.md\\n\\nBefore spawning wp-publisher:\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/verify_artifacts.py \\\\\\n --stage pre_wp --manifest \\\"$RUN_DIR/manifest.json\\\"\\n```\\n\\nAfter WP publish success **or** user says NO — terminal cleanup:\\n\\n```bash\\nbash ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/cleanup_run_artifacts.sh \\\\\\n --manifest \\\"$RUN_DIR/manifest.json\\\"\\n```\\n\\n### 8. Anchor validator — promote mismatch to error\\n\\nIn [workspace-writer/skills/validate_anchor_links.py](workspace-writer/skills/validate_anchor_links.py):\\n\\nWhen `research.json` is passed, \\\"source link not in research `source_urls`\\\" becomes an `ARTICLE_INVALID` error (not a warning). At least one body source URL must appear in current validated research. Triggers existing repair retry.\\n\\n### 9. Researcher diversity — Phase 2 (same delivery or follow-up)\\n\\n- [workspace-researcher/SOUL.md](workspace-researcher/SOUL.md): on `EXISTS`, pick next candidate (not just stop).\\n- History `add` also called after Step 4 Drive success (not only WP), so skipping WP still records the URL.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Root cause (technical, confirmed on disk)\\n\\n| Layer | Finding |\\n|-------|---------|\\n| Writer | Can overwrite `crypto-article-raw.md` correctly |\\n| Orchestrator Step 2 | Lines 158–178 of [SOUL.md](workspace-orchestrator/SOUL.md) update canonical; if Nexus skips bash, canonical stays stale |\\n| Step 4 / Step 6 | Read `/tmp/crypto-article.md` and global `/tmp/crypto-article.docx` — never raw |\\n| Step 0 | Symlinks only 4 paths; leaves `researcher-raw.txt`, `crypto-article-raw.md`, `article-structure.json`, `docx` as global real files |\\n\\nYour agent's Tests 4–6 confirmed: raw = SC, canonical = Canada, docx = Canada. Only one stale global file needed to break the whole publish.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n\\n1. **Split-state repro:** Set `article/raw.md` = SC, `article/final.md` = Canada; run `sync_article_from_raw.py` → final becomes SC; `post_sync` passes.\\n2. **Mismatch guard:** Skip sync; `pre_drive` must exit non-zero; pipeline stops.\\n3. **Full pipeline run:** Confirm logs show `ARTICLE_SYNCED` + `pre_drive ARTIFACTS_OK`; WP post H1 matches `research_validated.primary_headline`.\\n4. **Docx lineage:** Modify `final.md` after pandoc; `pre_wp` must catch `docx older than final.md`.\\n5. **Cleanup timing:** Run to Drive; confirm `$RUN_DIR` alive; say NO to WP; confirm cleanup runs and symlinks removed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\n- Tweet URL rescue, variable structure (already shipped)\\n- Full manifest state machine / resume / approval flow\\n- Phase 4 legacy symlink removal\\n- Researcher multi-candidate picker script\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Files to change\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| [workspace-orchestrator/SOUL.md](workspace-orchestrator/SOUL.md) | Step 0 → init_run; Steps 1–6 → manifest paths + gates + cleanup on terminal |\\n| `workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/` | 7 new scripts (init, manifest_paths, validate_research, sync, verify, update_manifest, cleanup) |\\n| [workspace-researcher/SOUL.md](workspace-researcher/SOUL.md) | Spawn path uses `$RUN_DIR/research/raw.json` |\\n| [workspace-writer/SOUL.md](workspace-writer/SOUL.md) | Spawn path uses `$RUN_DIR/article/raw.md`; reads validated + structure |\\n| [workspace-writer/skills/validate_anchor_links.py](workspace-writer/skills/validate_anchor_links.py) | Mismatch → error |\\n| [workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh](workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh) | Phase 2: optional manifest env override |\\n| [PIPELINE_ARCHITECTURE.md](PIPELINE_ARCHITECTURE.md) | Run-bundle layout + lineage table |\\n| [PIPELINE_DOCS/05_FILE_MANIFEST.md](PIPELINE_DOCS/05_FILE_MANIFEST.md) | New scripts + migration phases |\\n\\nNo changes to `openclaw.json` or agent list required.\\n\\\" --just say yes or halfyes-halfno or no\"}],\"timestamp\":1779347927887}}\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/agents/orchestrator/sessions/3d69fc49-c0a3-4f8a-ac4e-6e441c7d595d.checkpoint.f701932a-c8a8-48d6-9f48-a64b1009257c.jsonl-200-{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"c483af98\",\"parentId\":\"3d657487\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-21T07:19:42.099Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"yes\"}],\"api\":\"openai-completions\",\"provider\":\"local-bifrost\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"usage\":{\"input\":73853,\"output\":110,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":73963,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"stop\",\"timestamp\":1779347927904,\"responseId\":\"chatcmpl-DhryrEcaBHC4T9oVpmcRXyBAWEvNm\"}}\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/agents/orchestrator/sessions/3d69fc49-c0a3-4f8a-ac4e-6e441c7d595d.checkpoint.f701932a-c8a8-48d6-9f48-a64b1009257c.jsonl-201-{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"beade1f8\",\"parentId\":\"c483af98\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-21T07:32:44.740Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Sender (untrusted metadata):\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"label\\\": \\\"openclaw-control-ui\\\",\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"openclaw-control-ui\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n[Thu 2026-05-21 07:32 UTC] its done implementation of the plan everything should be fixed now can you test about this issue once again no changed will be made from you. only tests and report to me short\"}],\"timestamp\":1779348764706}}\n--\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/agents/orchestrator/sessions/29294ac6-86bb-489f-b6ce-fece2b90af6f.jsonl.deleted.2026-05-04T03-20-23.455Z-13-{\"type\":\"custom\",\"customType\":\"model-snapshot\",\"data\":{\"timestamp\":1777703413342,\"provider\":\"google-vertex\",\"modelApi\":\"google-vertex\",\"modelId\":\"gemini-2.0-flash\"},\"id\":\"15838c4a\",\"parentId\":\"295d519b\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-02T06:30:13.342Z\"}\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/agents/orchestrator/sessions/29294ac6-86bb-489f-b6ce-fece2b90af6f.jsonl.deleted.2026-05-04T03-20-23.455Z-14-{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"1dc689f4\",\"parentId\":\"15838c4a\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-02T06:30:13.401Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Run the crypto news pipeline.\"}],\"timestamp\":1777703413398}}\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/agents/orchestrator/sessions/29294ac6-86bb-489f-b6ce-fece2b90af6f.jsonl.deleted.2026-05-04T03-20-23.455Z:15:{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"747eff22\",\"parentId\":\"1dc689f4\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-02T06:30:16.463Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\